error[Z0401]: `event(year, never)` finds no treated row: `never` is NA wherever `year` is not
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | e.reg(y ~ event(year, never))
  |   ^^^ no unit is ever treated
  |
  = help: `treat` holds the period a unit was first treated in and `NA` for a unit never treated; an event study needs some of each
----
error[Z0401]: `event` needs `time` and `treat` of one type, both Int or both Date, but `year` is an Int and `t` is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | e.reg(y ~ event(year, t))
  |   ^^^ two kinds of time
  |
  = help: `treat` is the period a unit was first treated in, in the time variable's own type; `NA` marks a unit never treated
----
error[Z0401]: `event` is a term of a formula and has no value outside one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | event(year, treat)
  | ^^^^^ called outside a formula
  |
  = help: write it on the right of `~`: `y ~ event(year, treated_in)`, usually with `fe: unit + year`
